From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:16:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: q6voice: say what the session did

BRINGUP aid folded into the series while it is being brought up. The
driver reported nothing on the happy path, so a silent call could not be
told apart from a session that never started, one that was created
instead of joined, or a direction that never prepared -- and each of
those needs a different fix. Several real calls were spent guessing
between them.

Log the handles and whether each was joined or created, log a failure
with the ports it was attempted on, and log each direction as it
prepares.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice-dai.c |  4 ++++
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c     | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice-dai.c
index 4883b57af2ab..f921f9497137 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice-dai.c
@@ -89,6 +89,10 @@ static int q6voice_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	else
 		v->tx_port = port;
 
+	dev_info(component->dev, "%s prepared on port 0x%04x (rx=0x%04x tx=0x%04x)\n",
+		 substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK ?
+		 "playback" : "capture", port, v->rx_port, v->tx_port);
+
 	if (v->started || !v->rx_port || !v->tx_port)
 		return 0;
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
index a587a941885d..74c9fe4b6054 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
@@ -294,8 +294,17 @@ int q6voice_start(u16 rx_port, u16 tx_port)
 		goto out;
 
 	v->running = true;
+	dev_info(&v->mvm.adev->dev,
+		 "voice session up: mvm=0x%04x%s cvs=0x%04x%s cvp=0x%04x, rx=0x%04x tx=0x%04x\n",
+		 v->mvm.handle, v->mvm.joined ? " (joined)" : " (created)",
+		 v->cvs.handle, v->cvs.joined ? " (joined)" : " (created)",
+		 v->cvp.handle, rx_port, tx_port);
 	ret = 0;
 out:
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(&v->mvm.adev->dev,
+			"voice session failed at rx=0x%04x tx=0x%04x: %d\n",
+			rx_port, tx_port, ret);
 	mutex_unlock(&v->lock);
 
 	return ret;
@@ -334,6 +343,7 @@ int q6voice_stop(void)
 
 	v->cvp.handle = 0;
 	v->running = false;
+	dev_info(&v->mvm.adev->dev, "voice session down\n");
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&v->lock);
 
